        "title": "refactor(policy): split doctor evaluator modules",
        "body": "Closes #106295\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\n`extensions/policy/src/doctor/register.ts` had grown to roughly 5,600 lines and mixed registration, evaluation orchestration, policy-shape parsing, scoped-policy handling, evidence checks, sandbox checks, and runtime/file helpers. Routine maintenance required navigating one oversized module with many unrelated responsibilities.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nSplit the implementation into focused modules while retaining `register.ts` as the stable registration and public-export facade. The split preserves all 212 original top-level declarations, keeps the registration guard and hook wiring unchanged, and groups code by ownership: shapes, scope, evidence domains, runtime helpers, and evaluation orchestration.\n\nNo config, protocol, storage, SDK, or user-visible behavior changes.\n\nAI-assisted: yes (Codex). Four bounded autoreview passes covered foundations/shapes, finding evaluators, evaluation orchestration, and the facade; all returned no actionable findings.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible behavior change. Policy-doctor maintenance now happens in smaller, focused files with clearer dependency boundaries.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Mechanical declaration-equivalence check: 212/212 declarations preserved, with no missing, mismatched, or extra declarations before formatting.\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxdhhdw2rbr0q6zr46ehadp2`: `corepack pnpm test extensions/policy` — 6 files, 344 tests passed.\n- Same Testbox: `corepack pnpm tsgo:extensions`, `corepack pnpm tsgo:extensions:test`, `corepack pnpm lint:extensions`, and `corepack pnpm check:import-cycles` — passed; lint 0 warnings/errors and 0 runtime value cycles.\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\n- The repository-wide Plugin SDK baseline gate currently fails identically on canonical `main` at `0e520d68e7a925fdb6a9001e828f649478881df9`; this refactor does not touch Plugin SDK surfaces or generated baselines.\n",
